+### Accepted work and later research
+
+Current v2 closure derives from the exact task, current IntentRevision and immutable
+accepted outcome subject. Both production and expressly admitted negative research
+close that work. Contract reads distinguish `current_accepted`, historical
+`accepted` subjects, inert `legacy_accepted`, the raw migration `admission_open`
+flag, and effective `fresh_grant_eligible` contract eligibility.
+
+Completed work refuses new or cached consequential proposals, verification,
+artifact mutations, strategy/dependency changes, task mailbox mutations and fresh
+dispatch. Authenticated exact acceptance receipts remain immutable inspection,
+including after an authorized amendment. Re-keying an old proof never accepts the
+new intent. An authorized later-work admission fences generation immediately;
+assignment advances it again. Physical inspection, Stop, logs, Release and usage
+reconciliation retain their existing current-actor authority and original effect
+attribution. Task-ID waits are attention only; typed dependencies require exact
+revalidation. Cancellation and unknown usage never refund cumulative admissions.
+
+A research verifier Episode requires the exact admitted research contract and an
+independent current verifier. Its immutable captured input and supervised manifest
+pin intent, acceptance, policy, suite and environment before execution. Source
+amendments invalidate those dispatch pins. This path does not create a production
+candidate, report, or production verification binding. Production continues to
+require its immutable candidate and current measured gate. Research acceptance
+continues to validate its admitted evidence contract separately.
